\title{AdaptiveMCMCWorkflow: Teaching Adaptive MCMC Slowly and Explicitly}
\description{
\code{AdaptiveMCMCWorkflow} is a teaching package for adaptive random-walk MCMC.
The computational kernels live in C++ via \code{RcppArmadillo}, while the target
distributions, summaries, plots, and diagnostics live in R.
}
\details{
The package focuses on four algorithms:
\itemize{
\item basic Metropolis
\item Adaptive Metropolis (AM)
\item Robust Adaptive Metropolis (RAM)
\item Delayed Rejection Adaptive Metropolis (DRAM)
}

The package is built around a small set of sampler wrappers, target
constructors, summary helpers, and plotting helpers. In this source repo,
the simplest end-to-end demonstration is the script \code{run_adaptive_mcmc_demo.R}.

The package does not claim to prove general adaptive MCMC validity from
simulation. Instead, it provides empirical diagnostics that help a learner
think about ideas such as diminishing adaptation and containment.
}
